Seems fine now, with one exception. I am looking at `chan_req_send()` and this fragment:
```
	/* Keep a reference for resending in case of an error */
	err = chan_send(chan, net_buf_ref(req->buf), NULL);
	if (err) {
		net_buf_unref(req->buf);
		chan->req = NULL;
	}
```
seems suspicious to me. First of all "keep reference for resending in case of error" does not match what the code does: buffer will be referenced first, then unreferenced when error occurs - as a result buffer will be freed. Additionally properly sent buffer will be leaked, as all `chan_req_send` callers expect buffer to be freed/consumed.
